WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.129
"I wish I were invisible," said Jimmy.

2
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.604
The children were walking along in the growing darkness.

3
00:00:24.605 --> 00:00:26.765
"I'd be a burglar."

4
00:00:26.766 --> 00:00:31.709
"It's wrong to steal!" cried Kathleen and Mabel together.

5
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.411
"Then I'd be a detective," said Jimmy.

6
00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:37.872
"That's what I'll do,"

7
00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:41.406
said Gerald, who really was invisible.

8
00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:45.230
"Let's go to the police station and see if they need help."

9
00:00:45.231 --> 00:00:50.160
Outside the police station was a notice board.

10
00:00:50.161 --> 00:00:52.490
Two dogs had been lost.

11
00:00:52.491 --> 00:00:54.298
So had a purse.

12
00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:57.563
Gerald wasn't interested in any of that.

13
00:00:57.564 --> 00:01:01.756
Another notice announced that a mansion had been burglarized.

14
00:01:01.757 --> 00:01:06.083
Some silver candlesticks and serving dishes were stolen.

15
00:01:06.084 --> 00:01:10.255
"I'll catch those burglars!" Gerald decided.

16
00:01:10.256 --> 00:01:11.939
"There's Officer Johnson.

17
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.202
Go ask him what he knows about the crime."

18
00:01:15.203 --> 00:01:21.531
The visible children talked to the policeman, but he didn't have much to say.

19
00:01:21.532 --> 00:01:24.133
"Officer Johnson thinks he knows who did it.

20
00:01:24.134 --> 00:01:28.653
But he needs proof," Jimmy reported back to Gerald.

21
00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:32.850
"You're not much help," Gerald replied.

22
00:01:32.851 --> 00:01:36.342
"You didn't even find out how or when the silver was taken.

23
00:01:36.343 --> 00:01:39.168
Go home and eat your supper."

24
00:01:39.169 --> 00:01:41.140
"What will you do about supper?"

25
00:01:41.141 --> 00:01:45.046
Mabel asked Gerald as they started walking again.

26
00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:51.125
"I'm hoping one of you will buy me some buns."

27
00:01:51.126 --> 00:01:56.833
The children stopped outside the bakery, and Kathleen and Jimmy went inside.

28
00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:59.700
"Oh!" Mabel suddenly cried.

29
00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.529
"What's wrong?" asked Gerald.

30
00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:07.673
"I just remembered I left the window open in the treasure room.

31
00:02:07.674 --> 00:02:09.538
I have to go back right now.

32
00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:11.427
My aunt will be so angry!

33
00:02:11.428 --> 00:02:14.319
The treasure room door is locked from the inside.

34
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.881
She'll have to ask the gardener to get a ladder and climb through the window."

35
00:02:18.882 --> 00:02:26.887
"Don't worry," Gerald said. "I can climb through the window."

36
00:02:26.888 --> 00:02:36.994
They turned around while Jimmy and Kathleen continued home for supper.

37
00:02:36.995 --> 00:02:42.446
"Late again!" exclaimed Mademoiselle when the two of them arrived.

38
00:02:42.447 --> 00:02:45.253
"And where is Gerald?"

39
00:02:45.254 --> 00:02:50.073
"Uh . . . he has a headache," said Jimmy.

40
00:02:50.074 --> 00:02:52.723
"He went straight to bed."

41
00:02:52.724 --> 00:02:58.479
"Poor boy. I'll bring him some supper," said Mademoiselle.

42
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.885
"No, no," said Kathleen quickly.

43
00:03:01.886 --> 00:03:05.171
"He never eats when he has a headache."

44
00:03:05.172 --> 00:03:10.705
"Oh well," said Mademoiselle. "Hurry up and eat your supper."

45
00:03:10.706 --> 00:03:13.672
And she went back to reading some old letters.

46
00:03:13.673 --> 00:03:17.563
Meanwhile Gerald and Mabel arrived at the castle.

47
00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:21.976
Mabel knocked on the door the servants used.

48
00:03:21.977 --> 00:03:26.657
"Oh Mabel!" cried her aunt as she opened the door.

49
00:03:26.658 --> 00:03:29.120
"Thank goodness you're safe!"

50
00:03:29.121 --> 00:03:32.804
She gave Mabel a big hug.

51
00:03:32.805 --> 00:03:37.039
"I don't know what was wrong with me," said the aunt.

52
00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.173
"Yesterday I didn't care anything about you.

53
00:03:41.174 --> 00:03:45.757
The same thing happened when I got your note and when some children visited.

54
00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:51.396
But this afternoon I suddenly awoke from my trance and realized you were gone.

55
00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.503
It was awful!"

56
00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:58.280
Mabel's aunt pulled her into the castle and shut the door.

57
00:03:58.281 --> 00:04:00.109
"That was very strange,"

58
00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.542
said Gerald, who was left outside in the dark.

59
00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:06.376
"It seems like more magic to me."

60
00:04:06.377 --> 00:04:10.448
Gerald began looking for the open window of the treasure room.

61
00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:16.292
The castle gardens were so beautiful that he felt he was in another world.

62
00:04:16.293 --> 00:04:21.003
"Everything looks so different at night," he thought.

63
00:04:21.004 --> 00:04:25.287
Something white moved under a willow tree.

64
00:04:25.288 --> 00:04:30.346
The creature had a goat's horns and legs, but the head and arms of a boy.

65
00:04:30.347 --> 00:04:35.503
It stretched its legs, rolled on the grass, and then ran across the lawn.

66
00:04:35.504 --> 00:04:39.871
The most amazing thing was that Gerald was not afraid.

67
00:04:39.872 --> 00:04:42.984
There was still something white under the tree.

68
00:04:42.985 --> 00:04:47.317
Gerald moved closer and saw a pedestal for a statue.

69
00:04:47.318 --> 00:04:49.314
But nothing stood on it.

70
00:04:49.315 --> 00:04:52.626
"The statues . . . ," he murmured.

71
00:04:52.627 --> 00:04:58.766
Just then another statue walked out of the Temple of Flora and disappeared into some bushes.

72
00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:05.497
"They come alive!"
